-- Hateforge Quarry (map 808): the first plan for the Turtle custom dungeon, exported from dungeons/hateforge_quarry.json
-- (status 'draft (not mapped, not live-checked)') after the data census of PREP-HATEFORGE-QUARRY-2026-10-24.md. No live
-- run and no server: no row is hand-set; every position is a spawn row of the map's export.
--   turtle-agent plan-export --mmaps <map 808 mmaps> --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --approach-hops --rev <sha> \
--     --stamp 20261024020800 --out <dir> hateforge_quarry
-- 5 legs, 427 steps (158 pulls: 54 + 29 + 5 + 63 + 7; 264 moves, the 5 bosses), 433 rows. Plan check (turtle-agent
-- plan-check, the agent's mmaps): 2 of 348 points fail and 63 warnings (58 estimated patrol periods + the 5 detours of
-- the pack-in-a-lower-shelf pulls).
-- The two failures, both left for the GM mapping walk, neither invented:
--   * leg 0 boss High Foreman Bargul Blackhammer (60735) at -8304.88 -3442.24 194.45: his terrace above the quarry is a
--     SEPARATE navmesh network. The creature path 2570432 walks up to it (creature_movement: -8321.08 -3448.15 180.784,
--     -8323.71 -3452.3 182.523, -8309.45 -3460.42 194.425), but the mesh has floor polygons there and no link: from
--     the lower floor the nearest reachable point is 9.6 / 12.6 yd away, from the entrance / the last pull 21.7 yd (the
--     boss point snaps to a floor at 194.6). The plan marks the boss needs_walk. The walk tests the ramp; if it is not
--     walkable the leg needs a gm_cross (the exporter writes one as a move_direct, not tried live) or an off-mesh link.
--     Until then leg 0 ends short of the boss and the run stops there (the plan check fails and the run leader waits).
--   * leg 3 pull group 7: its pack stands on the shelf at z 167.5 and the path's look point is 11 yd above it (22 yd 3-D,
--     0.0 yd short of the 22 yd view): the stand is the mapping walk's first item on that shelf.
-- What the census fixed (before -> after, the numbers of PREP-HATEFORGE-QUARRY-2026-10-24.md section 7): 13 rows of a pack
-- split across two pull groups folded into their neighbour; every radius from the exporter's farthest member + 10 (which
-- reached 27 foreign mobs) to 2.5 yd off the group's own spawn rows; Broody 60715 out of its lone pull into Engineer
-- Figgles' boss.first (he stands 3.7 yd from the boss); the boss room's two rows (6 + 1 units, 2.2 yd apart) merged into
-- one 7-unit pull and moved last, before the boss; 63 patrol blocks from creature_movement (34 spawns patrol, Corrosis
-- 60829 among them; a block sits on every pull a patrol's path enters and on every pull of a patrolling member; the run
-- leader's rows carry none). Unit lists: no fleers (no EventAI event for any map-808 creature), kill_first 60718 (healer,
-- Greater Heal 10965) 60726 (Twilight Shadow) 60723 (Hooked Net) 60712 60738, cc_priority 60717 60720 60719 60725 (the
-- polymorphable humanoid casters), no_cc the mechanical/elemental/undead-type units the run leader must not pick.
-- Not in the rows: no_cc, summoned_kill_first, the patrols, needs_walk, the draft status, the level band and the hire
-- composition. Har'gesh Doomcaller's phase two (2 Faceless Terror 60738 per player, immune until they die) and the
-- Engineer's summoned Decoy Dragonlings are the run leader's fight; no spawn row names them.
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql. The boss rows
-- of map 808 are added at the end, DELETE scoped to this plan's own five entries (the map has no other plan).
--
-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

-- hateforge_quarry: map 808, 5 legs, 427 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'hateforge_quarry';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'hateforge_quarry';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'hateforge_quarry';

-- The map-808 boss rows (ai_dungeon_boss, the pattern of 20261021114931_world.sql). The exporter does not write this table; the
-- five rows are the plan's boss entries, all rank 1 in creature_template, entry-scoped so another plan of map 808 would keep its own.
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_boss` WHERE `map` IN (808) AND `entry` IN (60735, 60829, 60737, 60736, 60734);
